      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2e2ab863aa6f7311d53d03|full_name}: Indeed, its laying play mode limits head rotation for the player. However, since the controller can change the orientation of the avatar body, I think it is possible to complement the movement of the avatar.\nI have no physical disabilities, but I try not to move my neck. This is because the weight of the HMD is relatively heavy and there is a risk of damaging the neck joint. Instead of turning the head, the controller is turning the avatar's body.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
